EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::AcceptOwnership
├── when caller is not pending owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is pending owner
    └── it should transfer ownership

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::CcipReceive
├── when caller is not ccipRouter
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is ccipRouter
    ├── when message was already executed
    │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
    │   └── it should keep executedMessage set
    └── when message was not executed
        ├── when message has no tokens
        │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
        │   └── it should update executedMessage
        ├── when message has more than max tokens
        │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
        │   ├── it should update executedMessage
        │   └── it should escrow message tokens
        ├── when message has two tokens
        │   ├── when tokens are duplicated
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
        │   │   ├── it should update executedMessage
        │   │   └── it should escrow message tokens
        │   ├── when a token amount is zero
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
        │   │   └── it should update executedMessage
        │   ├── when message data is malformed
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
        │   │   ├── it should update executedMessage
        │   │   └── it should escrow message tokens
        │   ├── when message data receiver is zero address
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
        │   │   ├── it should update executedMessage
        │   │   └── it should escrow message tokens
        │   ├── when contract is paused
        │   │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
        │   │   ├── it should update executedMessage
        │   │   └── it should safe transfer both token amounts to receiver
        │   ├── when shortcut execution succeeded
        │   │   ├── it should emit ShortcutExecutionSuccessful
        │   │   ├── it should update executedMessage
        │   │   └── it should apply shortcut state changes via routeMulti
        │   └── when shortcut execution failed
        │       ├── it should emit ShortcutExecutionFailed
        │       ├── it should update executedMessage
        │       └── it should safe transfer both token amounts to receiver
        └── when message has single token
            ├── when message token amount is zero
            │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
            │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
            │   └── it should update executedMessage
            ├── when message data is malformed
            │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
            │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
            │   ├── it should update executedMessage
            │   └── it should escrow message token
            ├── when message data receiver is zero address
            │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
            │   ├── it should emit MessageQuarantined
            │   ├── it should update executedMessage
            │   └── it should escrow message token
            ├── when contract is paused
            │   ├── it should emit MessageValidationFailed
            │   ├── it should update executedMessage
            │   └── it should safe transfer token amount to receiver
            ├── when shortcut execution succeeded
            │   ├── it should emit ShortcutExecutionSuccessful
            │   ├── it should update executedMessage
            │   └── it should apply shortcut state changes via routeSingle
            └── when shortcut execution failed
                ├── it should emit ShortcutExecutionFailed
                ├── it should update executedMessage
                └── it should safe transfer token amount to receiver

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::Constructor
└── when deployed
    ├── it should set owner
    ├── it should set ccipRouter
    └── it should set ensoRouter

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::Execute
├── when caller is not self
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is self
    ├── when tokens length is below min
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when tokens length exceeds max
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when shortcut execution failed
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when shortcut execution succeeded
        ├── when single token
        │   └── it should apply shortcut state changes via routeSingle
        └── when two tokens
            └── it should apply shortcut state changes via routeMulti

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::GetEnsoRouter
└── it should return EnsoRouter address

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::Pause
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    └── it should pause the contract

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::RecoverTokens
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    ├── it should safe transfer amount to recipient
    └── it should emit TokensRecovered

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::RenounceOwnership
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    └── it should transfer ownership to zero address

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::SupportsInterface
├── when interfaceId is type IAny2EVMMessageReceiver
│   └── it should return true
└── when interfaceId is not type IAny2EVMMessageReceiver
    ├── when interfaceId is type IERC165
    │   └── it should return true
    └── when interfaceId is not type IERC165
        └── it should return false

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::TransferOwnership
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    └── it should start ownership transfer

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::TypeAndVersion
└── it should return current type and semantic version

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::Unpause
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    └── it should unpause the contract

EnsoCCIPReceiverV2::WasMessageExecuted
└── it should return whether message was executed
